sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgb(254,205,211) People
    actor U as User
  end
  box rgb(191,219,254) Browser
    participant B as Chat page
  end
  box rgb(187,247,208) Python server moodle_llm_chat
    participant C as Chat service websocket
    participant A as Agent runner LangGraph
    participant T as Tools and access client
    participant DB as Encrypted store and quota
  end
  box rgb(221,214,254) LLM provider
    participant LLM as Chat model
  end
  box rgb(253,240,138) Moodle plugin local_llmchat
    participant CB as callback.php
  end
  box rgb(254,215,170) Moodle
    participant Core as Moodle core roles and availability
  end

  U->>B: types a question
  B->>C: send frame with a fresh chat token
  C->>C: verify token and apply the burst limit
  C->>DB: check quota, create conversation and turn, store the user message
  C-->>B: accepted

  par naming a new conversation
    C->>LLM: utility model proposes a short title
    LLM-->>C: title
    C-->>B: title event
  and the answer
    C->>A: run the turn with the user's scope and the saved history
    A->>A: build tools and system prompt for this user only
    loop until a final answer, the step limit or the token budget forces one
      A->>LLM: messages and tool definitions
      LLM-->>A: streamed thinking, text and tool calls
      A-->>C: delta events
      C-->>B: streamed text
      opt the model calls a tool such as search_content or read_file
        A->>T: run the tool
        T->>DB: search or read, restricted to modules in the token scope
        DB-->>T: matching chunks, decrypted
        rect rgba(34,139,230,0.10)
          Note over T,Core: LIVE ACCESS CHECK - is the user still allowed to read these modules right now
          T->>CB: POST check with bearer site secret and the module ids, cached 60 s, circuit breaker after 3 failures
          CB->>Core: which of these modules are visible to this user now
          Core-->>CB: visible subset
          CB-->>T: allowed module ids
        end
        alt Moodle cannot be reached
          T-->>A: error result, nothing is shown to the model
        else access confirmed
          T-->>A: numbered hits with citations and display blocks
        end
        A-->>C: tool call and tool result events
        C-->>B: tool card with sources
      end
      A-->>C: token usage
      C->>DB: record tokens and check the turn budget
    end
    A-->>C: final answer with citations
  end

  C->>DB: store events, save citations, mark the turn done, prune old checkpoints
  C-->>B: final event
  B-->>U: answer with clickable source cards
